From 5c54a590d79ee0cc9ef6c3bf7b35928f17aef02e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:04:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] Carry the keyboard light loop under its own name

Omarchy's Mac checks (omarchy-m-test input.ambient-light and
input.auto-keyboard-light) look for omarchy-brightness-keyboard-auto and
its user unit, the team's loop from omarchy-mac. The extraction left it
out, so the keyboard followed the room only through
omarchy-mac-brightness-auto and both checks failed by name.

Carry Scott Jones's helper and unit under their names, with two
changes: a Mac whose brightness table has KBD_CURVE follows that curve
(the MacBook Pro 14" M4: macOS's keyboard curve, 24 % dark, 69 % at
70-160 lux, never off), and an off that stock omarchy-brightness-keyboard
recorded (the lock's blank, idle) is not taken as the user's choice,
while keys stepped to off stay off until the room changes enough. The
keyboard half leaves omarchy-mac-brightness-auto, so one loop drives the
keyboard.
